<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GoPackageInitialization - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gopackageinitialization/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 20:06:49 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gopackageinitialization/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 204</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_204/</link><pubDate>Wed, 05 Mar 2025 11:58:52 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_204/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Regarding the &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; function, which of the following statements are correct:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. A package can contain multiple &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; functions;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. When the program runs, &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; functions of dependent packages are executed first, then &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; functions within the &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; package;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. The &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; package cannot have &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; functions;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;D. An &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; function can be called by other functions;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A, B&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here are a few things to note about &lt;code&gt;init()&lt;/code&gt; functions:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 200</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_200/</link><pubDate>Sat, 01 Mar 2025 02:08:44 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_200/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;When is the init() function executed?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Answer: &lt;code&gt;init()&lt;/code&gt; is executed before the &lt;code&gt;main()&lt;/code&gt; function.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Summary in one sentence: &lt;code&gt;import –&amp;gt; const –&amp;gt; var –&amp;gt; init() –&amp;gt; main()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If there are multiple init functions, the situation varies.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 class="heading-element" id="execution-order-of-init-in-a-single-source-file"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Execution Order of init in a Single Source File&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#execution-order-of-init-in-a-single-source-file" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Conclusion: &lt;code&gt;The execution order of init functions within the same source file is consistent with their 